==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|movers and shakers}}

# {{lb|en|usually|in the plural}} Someone who has [[power]] and [[influence]] in a [[field]] or [[activity]]; one who [[accomplish]]es tasks, who gets things done.
#: {{ux|en|The sales team sought to talk to the '''movers and shakers''' within an organization, rather than to their underlings.}}
#: {{ux|en|He really is a '''mover and a shaker''' in those circles.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 December 29|author=Stephen Roberts|title=Stories and Facts behind railway plaques: Reading (1840)|journal=RAIL|issue=947|page=54|text=People such as William James and the Stephensons (with whom he collaborated) may have been the '''movers and shakers''' of the early railways, but there was other, less exalted bods who constructed all the paraphernalia - including stations.}}

